# Every prerendered page is a real file on disk, but the SPA catch-all below
# rewrites anything unmatched to the root landing. Each prerendered route
# therefore needs an explicit rule ABOVE the catch-all, or a crawler can be
# served the landing page (or a redirect it can't resolve) instead of the page
# it asked for. Both the bare and trailing-slash forms are listed so the two
# spellings resolve identically rather than bouncing between each other.
/en            /en/index.html            200
/en/           /en/index.html            200
/guide         /guide/index.html         200
/guide/        /guide/index.html         200
/exam/:id/     /exam/:id/index.html      200
/exam/:id      /exam/:id/index.html      200
/*             /index.html               200
